"<div id=""mindx-fmla-clinician-tool"">

<h2>FMLA Documentation Readiness Estimator</h2>

<div class=""subtitle"">
Review whether you have the clinical information and documentation needed to consider completing FMLA-related paperwork for a client.
</div>


<!-- Question 1 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Do you have an established clinical relationship with the client?
</label>

<select id=""q1"">

<option value=""0"">
No / Very limited contact
</option>

<option value=""1"">
Some contact, but limited clinical history
</option>

<option value=""2"">
Established treatment relationship
</option>

<option value=""3"">
Established relationship with sufficient clinical history
</option>

</select>

</div>


<!-- Question 2 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Do you have sufficient clinical information about the condition affecting the client's functioning?
</label>

<select id=""q2"">

<option value=""0"">
No
</option>

<option value=""1"">
Limited information
</option>

<option value=""2"">
Generally sufficient
</option>

<option value=""3"">
Well documented
</option>

</select>

</div>


<!-- Question 3 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Can you clearly describe the client's functional limitations related to work or other major life activities?
</label>

<select id=""q3"">

<option value=""0"">
Not at this time
</option>

<option value=""1"">
Some limitations are apparent
</option>

<option value=""2"">
Limitations are reasonably clear
</option>

<option value=""3"">
Limitations are clearly documented
</option>

</select>

</div>


<!-- Question 4 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Have you documented the relevant symptoms, clinical observations, and their impact on functioning?
</label>

<select id=""q4"">

<option value=""0"">
No
</option>

<option value=""1"">
Partially
</option>

<option value=""2"">
Mostly
</option>

<option value=""3"">
Yes, adequately documented
</option>

</select>

</div>


<!-- Question 5 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Can you clinically describe the expected frequency and/or duration of the client's impairment or treatment needs?
</label>

<select id=""q5"">

<option value=""0"">
No
</option>

<option value=""1"">
Unclear at this time
</option>

<option value=""2"">
I have a reasonable clinical estimate
</option>

<option value=""3"">
Clearly supported by the clinical record
</option>

</select>

</div>


<!-- Question 6 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Have you reviewed the specific paperwork or information requested?
</label>

<select id=""q6"">

<option value=""0"">
No
</option>

<option value=""1"">
I know generally what is being requested
</option>

<option value=""2"">
I have reviewed the relevant sections
</option>

<option value=""3"">
I have reviewed the form and understand the information requested
</option>

</select>

</div>


<!-- Question 7 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Is the requested information within your professional scope and based on your clinical knowledge?
</label>

<select id=""q7"">

<option value=""0"">
No / Unclear
</option>

<option value=""1"">
Some portions may require clarification
</option>

<option value=""2"">
Generally within my scope
</option>

<option value=""3"">
Clearly within my scope and clinical expertise
</option>

</select>

</div>


<!-- Question 8 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Have you obtained any required client authorization or release of information?
</label>

<select id=""q8"">

<option value=""0"">
No
</option>

<option value=""1"">
Not yet / unclear
</option>

<option value=""2"">
Authorization is being addressed
</option>

<option value=""3"">
Appropriate authorization is documented
</option>

</select>

</div>


<!-- Question 9 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Does the clinical record reasonably support the information you would provide?
</label>

<select id=""q9"">

<option value=""0"">
No
</option>

<option value=""1"">
Some information is supported
</option>

<option value=""2"">
Most information is supported
</option>

<option value=""3"">
The requested information is well supported
</option>

</select>

</div>


<!-- Question 10 -->

<div class=""question"">

<label>
Have you considered whether additional assessment or documentation is needed before completing the form?
</label>

<select id=""q10"">

<option value=""0"">
I have not considered this
</option>

<option value=""1"">
I may need additional information
</option>

<option value=""2"">
I have reviewed what may be needed
</option>

<option value=""3"">
I have sufficient information or have identified the remaining items
</option>

</select>

</div>


<button
type=""button""
onclick=""estimateFMLAReadiness()"">

Check Documentation Readiness

</button>


<div id=""fmlaClinicianResult""></div>


<div class=""note"">

This tool is for clinical workflow and documentation planning only. It does not determine FMLA eligibility, certify that leave is medically necessary, or provide legal advice. FMLA requirements and documentation standards may vary based on the circumstances. Follow applicable laws, regulations, professional standards, employer forms, and your organization's policies.

</div>

</div>


